Let $X$ denote the diameter of an armored electric cable and $Y$ denote the diameter of the ceramic mold that makes the cable. Both $X$ and $Y$ are scaled so that they range between 0 and 1. Suppose that $X$ and $Y$ have the joint density function given by:

\[
f(x,y) = \begin{cases} 
\frac{1}{y}, & 0 < x < y < 1 \\
0, & \text{elsewhere}
\end{cases}
\]

Find the probability $P(X+Y > 1/2)$. Provide your answer to four decimal places.

For a triangle with side lengths \(a, b, c\) and area equal to \(\frac{1}{4}\) where the circumradius is 1, if \[ s = \sqrt{a} + \sqrt{b} + \sqrt{c}, \quad t = \frac{1}{a} + \frac{1}{b} + \frac{1}{c}, \] what is the relationship between \(s\) and \(t\)?

(A) \(s > t\);  
(B) \(s = t\);  
(C) \(s < t\);  
(D) Cannot be determined.

Consider a tetrahedron where one edge has a length of \( x \) and the remaining edges have a length of 1. The volume of this tetrahedron is given by the function \( F(x) \). Determine the nature of the function \( F(x) \) over its domain:

(A) It is an increasing function but has no maximum value;
(B) It is an increasing function and has a maximum value;
(C) It is not an increasing function and has no maximum value;
(D) It is not an increasing function but has a maximum value.

